WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.534 --> 00:00:02.267
-Today is Friday and that's
usually when I catch up

00:00:02.267 --> 00:00:03.367
on some personal stuff.

00:00:03.367 --> 00:00:05.434
I check my inbox,
I return some emails,

00:00:05.434 --> 00:00:07.300
and, of course,
I send out thank-you notes.

00:00:07.300 --> 00:00:09.567
[ Cheering and applause ]
And I was just running
a bit behind.

00:00:09.567 --> 00:00:10.834
I was just wondering,
if you guys don't mind,

00:00:10.834 --> 00:00:12.601
can I write out my weekly
thank-you notes right now,

00:00:12.601 --> 00:00:13.400
for you guys that are here?

00:00:13.400 --> 00:00:14.634
[ Cheering and applause ]

00:00:14.634 --> 00:00:16.267
Appreciate that.
James, can I get some

00:00:16.267 --> 00:00:17.667
thank-you note writing music,
please?

00:00:17.667 --> 00:00:19.100
[ Playing tender tune ]

00:00:19.100 --> 00:00:20.801
[ Laughter ]
-Wow. Looks like Smooth --

00:00:20.801 --> 00:00:22.033
-Smooth Jeffrey, yeah, he does,

00:00:22.033 --> 00:00:23.968
a little bit.
[ Laughter ]

00:00:23.968 --> 00:00:26.501
-Smooth Jeffrey?
-Yeah, I know. Smooth Jeffrey.

00:00:26.501 --> 00:00:27.534
[ Laughter ]

00:00:27.534 --> 00:00:28.701
-He's wearing
the wrong pants, though.

00:00:28.701 --> 00:00:30.601
-Yeah.
[ Laughter ]

00:00:30.601 --> 00:00:31.701
♪♪

00:00:31.701 --> 00:00:33.400
Thank you, Apple,

00:00:33.400 --> 00:00:35.767
for officially
discontinuing the iPod.

00:00:35.767 --> 00:00:36.901
Or, as it's also known,

00:00:36.901 --> 00:00:38.868
going to the big junk drawer
in the sky.

00:00:38.868 --> 00:00:41.767
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:00:43.634 --> 00:00:45.400
I still got mine.
-Yeah.

00:00:45.400 --> 00:00:46.367
It's not charged?

00:00:46.367 --> 00:00:47.901
-No.
[ Laughter ]

00:00:47.901 --> 00:00:49.000
♪♪

00:00:49.000 --> 00:00:50.667
Thank you, Subway announcing

00:00:50.667 --> 00:00:52.434
they're facing a meat shortage,

00:00:52.434 --> 00:00:55.133
for making every Arby's ad
feel like a ransom note.

00:00:55.133 --> 00:00:58.067
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:01:02.501 --> 00:01:04.000
"What does it say?"

00:01:04.000 --> 00:01:05.701
It says, "We have the meats."

00:01:05.701 --> 00:01:06.767
[ Laughter ]

00:01:06.767 --> 00:01:08.801
-[ Baritone ]
We have the meats.

00:01:08.801 --> 00:01:10.167
♪♪
[ Laughter ]

00:01:10.167 --> 00:01:13.234
Thank you, new trailer
for "Avatar" 2,

00:01:13.234 --> 00:01:14.501
for showing us
what it would look like

00:01:14.501 --> 00:01:16.501
if the Smurfs got really
into CrossFit.

00:01:16.501 --> 00:01:19.467
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:01:21.334 --> 00:01:22.501
-Hoo hoo hoo!

00:01:22.501 --> 00:01:25.434
[ Laughter ]

00:01:25.501 --> 00:01:26.634
♪♪
[ Laughter ]

00:01:26.634 --> 00:01:28.901
Thank you, estate sales,

00:01:28.901 --> 00:01:30.434
for being a classy way to say,

00:01:30.434 --> 00:01:32.367
"Who wants to buy
some haunted furniture?"

00:01:32.367 --> 00:01:34.734
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:01:38.834 --> 00:01:40.000
♪♪
[ Laughter ]

00:01:40.000 --> 00:01:41.701
Thank you, sushi,

00:01:41.701 --> 00:01:44.234
for not being called
Fish Roll-Ups. Oh, that's --

00:01:44.234 --> 00:01:45.801
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:01:45.801 --> 00:01:47.100
It's an option.
-Yeah.

00:01:47.100 --> 00:01:48.133
-It's an option.

00:01:50.167 --> 00:01:51.367
♪♪
[ Laughter ]

00:01:51.367 --> 00:01:53.634
Thank you, Boston Celtics,

00:01:53.634 --> 00:01:54.767
for having a logo that says,

00:01:54.767 --> 00:01:56.601
"The key to being good
at basketball is

00:01:56.601 --> 00:01:58.868
smoking, using a cane,
and having a beer belly."

00:01:58.868 --> 00:02:01.868
[ Laughter, cheering,
and applause ]

00:02:06.000 --> 00:02:07.200
♪♪
[ Laughter ]

00:02:07.200 --> 00:02:09.534
Thank you, Friday the 13th,

00:02:09.534 --> 00:02:11.601
or, as millennial
Jason Voorhees calls you,

00:02:11.601 --> 00:02:12.934
Fri-yay the 13th.

00:02:12.934 --> 00:02:14.834
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:02:14.834 --> 00:02:16.467
♪♪

00:02:18.100 --> 00:02:21.033
[ Laughter ]

00:02:22.300 --> 00:02:23.467
♪♪

00:02:23.467 --> 00:02:24.534
Thank you --

00:02:24.534 --> 00:02:27.300
[ Laughter ]

00:02:27.300 --> 00:02:29.567
I'm sorry, Higgins.
I heard you laughing.

00:02:29.567 --> 00:02:30.968
[ Laughter ]

00:02:30.968 --> 00:02:33.901
[ Laughing helplessly ]

00:02:39.434 --> 00:02:41.067
-Oh!

00:02:41.067 --> 00:02:43.667
Oh!

00:02:43.667 --> 00:02:44.868
We got it.

00:02:44.868 --> 00:02:46.634
[ Laughter ]
Oh.

00:02:46.634 --> 00:02:47.767
La la la la.
-Did you say you saw something?

00:02:47.767 --> 00:02:51.000
-Yes. I saw something.
[ Laughter ]

00:02:51.000 --> 00:02:52.968
Millennials, so he's like --
-Yeah, yeah, Fri-yay.

00:02:52.968 --> 00:02:54.334
He says, "Fri-yay the 13th,"
right?

00:02:54.334 --> 00:02:55.567
-Yeah, so he has like
a skateboard,

00:02:55.567 --> 00:02:57.868
a backwards baseball hat.
-Jason Voorhees, yeah,

00:02:57.868 --> 00:02:59.968
he's got a back--
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:02:59.968 --> 00:03:04.934
♪♪

00:03:06.200 --> 00:03:07.701
He's got a skateboard, too.

00:03:07.701 --> 00:03:10.767
[ Laughter ]

00:03:14.267 --> 00:03:15.267
♪♪
[ Laughter ]

00:03:15.267 --> 00:03:17.801
Thank you, garden hoses,

00:03:17.801 --> 00:03:19.767
for having two speeds --
barely trickling

00:03:19.767 --> 00:03:21.801
or Hurricane Harper.
It's like, "Wow!"

00:03:21.801 --> 00:03:24.734
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:03:27.400 --> 00:03:28.400
♪♪

00:03:28.400 --> 00:03:30.367
Thank you, cocktail shakers,

00:03:30.367 --> 00:03:32.267
for being maracas
for alcoholics.

00:03:32.267 --> 00:03:33.701
[ Laughter and applause ]
Hey, there you have it.

00:03:33.701 --> 00:03:35.133
[ Cheering and applause ]
Those are my "Thank You Notes."

